# Version control
# .git/ is intentionally NOT excluded: setuptools_scm (see pyproject.toml's
# [tool.setuptools_scm]) needs it -- and a *complete*, non-sparse working
# tree next to it -- in the builder stage to derive the package version
# from the nearest git tag via `git describe`, the same way a local
# `pip install -e .` does. `git describe --dirty` diffs the working tree
# against the index; if tests/, examples/, .github/ etc. were excluded
# here the way they used to be, git would see them as "deleted" and the
# build would always resolve a dirty/guessed version even from a clean,
# exactly-tagged commit. None of this reaches the final runtime image --
# Dockerfile's runtime stage only COPYs the builder's compiled /install
# output and src/, never the raw context.

# Python artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Virtual environment
.venv/
venv/

# Credentials – NEVER copy into image. These are the actual filenames this
# project's Tibber backend uses (see .gitignore) -- NOT the old
# src/config.json/src/tokenstore.json names from the removed carconnectivity
# backend, which don't exist here anymore and excluding them protected
# nothing. Kept in sync with .gitignore's own credential patterns (that
# file is the reference; a real secret was found missing from here twice
# in a row while wiring this up -- see git history) rather than
# re-deriving similar-looking patterns by hand again.
src/tibber_config.json
tibber_tokens.json
**/*tibber_tokens.json
**/*tibber_tokens.json.lock
.env
**/*.env
# local/ is gitignored as a scratch/backup directory for rescued secrets
# (see .gitignore) -- confirmed live to contain a real .env and a real
# tibber_tokens.json copy, neither of which the patterns above alone would
# have caught nested under it.
local/
/tmp/tokenstore*
logs/

# Development / editor
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo

# Docs / examples: not excluded from the build CONTEXT (see .git/ note
# above -- their absence would falsely mark the tree dirty), but the
# runtime image never gets them either way since Dockerfile only COPYs
# src/ and the builder's compiled /install output into it.
tmp/
